if GameState.get_flag("act1/talked_to_blacksmith") == true:
	The blacksmith grunts a greeting without looking up from the anvil. "Mind the mist out there, lad. Something feels off today."
	jump end
The blacksmith straightens from the anvil, broad as a door, and wipes his hands down his apron. "So. Today is the day."
He nods toward the stables. "Your mare is shod and sound. I put the good nails in her, not the cheap ones."
- "Thank you. Truly."
	He waves it off and busies himself with a hammer that did not need moving.
- "How much do I owe you?"
	He looks at you as though you have insulted his mother, and turns back to the anvil.
He is quiet a moment. Then, lower, without turning around. He holds out your sword, the edge bright enough to shave with. "Next time I see you I want this sword to be dull. You hear me boy? Dull!"
[signal arg="set_flag act1/talked_to_blacksmith"]
label end